  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `ctx.navigate` is not supplied, when `handleEmail` runs, then it still sets `window.location.href` to the mailto: URL (no behavior change for production callers).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `ctx.navigate` is supplied in a test, when `handleEmail` runs with ≥1 selected todo, then the injected function receives the mailto: URL with correctly-encoded subject/body, and no `.skip` remains on the test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the full SmartTodo Jest suite, when it runs, then it reports 78/78 passing (zero skipped, zero failing).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given two overlapping `handlePickerSelect` calls where the earlier call's `resolveRecordType` resolves after the later call already completed, then `onRecordTypeChanged` reflects only the later (winning) selection — the stale resolution is a no-op (S1).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given `resolveRecordType` rejects during the picker-select flow, then `console.error` (not `console.warn`) is invoked with the failure (N1).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no `ControlManifest.Input.xml` version bump or PCF redeploy occurs as part of this task — S1/N1 land in source only, deferred to the next real version bump.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Line numbers cited in this POML (1259 for N1's `console.warn`, 1272 for the adjacent `console.error`) are current as of 2026-08-15 and may have shifted by execution time — re-locate by message text (`'resolveRecordType for output notify failed:'` / `'handlePickerSelect error:'`) rather than trusting the literal line numbers. The design-doc's function name `handleSelectRecord` is stale — the current function is `handlePickerSelect` (renamed by the v1.4.0 SRFR-045 AssociationResolver-consolidation commit); this is a naming drift, not a different function.</notes>

